dsh-task-runner is a local composite integration, not an official DeepSeek product.

Includes server components from:
- MichengAI/dsh-pua 0.3.27 (Apache-2.0), with its LICENSE and NOTICE under vendor/pua/.
- GreenLv/dsh-completion-guard 0.9.0 (Apache-2.0), local protocol-repair source commit
  d7c4f80860f2ce702741701db33784bc7b7d78c9, license vendor/GUARD-LICENSE.
- MoonCoder-HAPPY/SpecWorkflow npm 0.1.1 (MIT, copyright 2026 jingdan):
  unchanged to-grill and to-spec skills and references under vendor/specworkflow/.
  License and file provenance are included there. specworkflow.mjs ports their
  registration to the installed DSH 0.2.0-rc.2 SDK and exposes only these stages.

Modifications: relative package-local completion bridge imports, per-session
frozen task profiles, independent snapshot acceptance, completion/candidate/Goal
certificate binding, command/CLI launch, and bounded task lifetime. Version 0.2.1 adds locked GitHub installation
identity validation for non-critical direct plugins without changing Host SDK
registry integrity, byte or route qualification.
The original component authors do not endorse these modifications.
Base file hashes are recorded in vendor/base-provenance.json.
